        "char_primordial_origin_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Rumor Cage, Fang Yuan reads Rumors Become Tigers as information path unified with human path, drawing on the grudge of Central Continent’s mortals, and calls that similar to the people’s accusation killer move earlier.",
      "chapters": [
        1700
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grudge-and-human-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_rumor_cage",
        "move_rumors_become_tigers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later names people’s accusation a human path killer move that is getting stronger, and judges that the more times he shows up in Central Continent and the longer he stays, the stronger it becomes. He also judges that he cannot resolve people’s accusation using Emperor Yama.",
      "chapters": [
        1703
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "grudge-and-human-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_emperor_yama"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Above Emperor City, Fang Yuan stacks more than ten immortal methods on himself and can barely defend against the investigative power of people’s accusation; he lacks human path methods, and treats that partial block as already satisfactory.",
